{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sporting-witting-pittabird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13)\n'One source of contention for CI runners in this project is the reconciler bridge job and canary. let's double the time between runs for both jobs and for both fallback and the chained reconciler invocation.'\n\n## Context\nRunner-contention analysis (ticket dotted-uncheery-dunnart / sunbear AC2 evidence): 609 workflow_dispatch runs on main in ~33h were the Verified-lane starvation driver; the reconcile-bridge self-rescheduling chain is the dominant dispatch source.\n\n## Work — double all four intervals\n1. .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml cron backstop: '*/20 * * * *' -> a uniform 40-minute schedule (cron cannot express uniform 40-min in one entry; use the three-entry 2-hour-cycle form: '0 0-23/2 * * *', '40 0-23/2 * * *', '20 1-23/2 * * *' — verify GitHub Actions accepts multiple cron entries here, it does).\n2. reconcile-bridge.yml self-rescheduling chain (the workflow_dispatch re-seed around lines 291-316): double the inter-invocation delay knob (find the sleep/defer that paces the chain; if the chain is back-to-back with no delay, introduce the doubled pacing the comment block describes rather than leaving it near-continuous).\n3. .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml: '0 * * * *' hourly -> every 2 hours.\n4. Any in-workflow fallback interval constants tied to the above (the comment at reconcile-bridge.yml:21 calls the cron 'a backstop that re-seeds the chain' — keep that relationship intact at the doubled cadence).\n\n## Constraints\n- Update every comment that names the old cadence ('*/20', 'hourly') — the workflow's own documentation must stay truthful.\n- Check tests pinning cron literals: sunbear's new test_ci_tickets_push_policy pins five cron literals — update it; also test_ci_workflow_parity / provider matrix docs if they name cadences.\n- Reconciliation worst-case latency doubles (20->40 min backstop): note it in docs/ci-provider-matrix.md or wherever the cadence is documented.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Bridge backstop cron fires at a uniform 40-minute cadence; canary at 2-hourly.\n- [ ] The chain's inter-invocation pacing is doubled and the workflow comments name the new numbers.\n- [ ] All cadence-pinning tests and docs updated; full gate set green.","id":"f59a-2d16-68c5-450c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Halve reconciler bridge and canary run cadence"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786614086778616001,"uuid":"3a93f855-7e83-422a-84e2-d4ac08356e4c"}